    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive anchor. With an elite efficiency score of 82.126, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an ideal matchup against Trevor Rogers; the combination of favorable park factors and the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which significantly bolsters his stolen base upside\u2014makes him the primary target to catalyze our production. **Trea Turner** (73.89) and **Kyle Schwarber** (70.57) also provide high-floor value against Singer, with both hitters maintaining strong order positions and positive park adjustments that outweigh the standard platoon tax. **Casey Schmitt** remains a high-upside play at 63.20; despite the pending official lineup, the projected wind-out conditions and a favorable matchup against Ryan Feltner position him to outperform his baseline projection.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, specifically with **Lars Nootbaar** (43.93), whose start is precarious due to a 38% rain risk and a difficult encounter with a sub-3.00 xERA arm. While **Chase Meidroth** (44.88) holds a similar score, his role as the leadoff hitter keeps him in the lineup despite facing an elite pitcher in Sandoval. **Luke Raley** (55.33) fell just shy of the \"Strong\" start threshold but remains in the lineup due to his platoon advantage and solid SP-skill pairing. The most difficult bench decision involved evaluating our utility depth, but the current configuration maximizes our sprint-speed requirements\u2014a premium for the Zebras\u2014while we await the return of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Christian Yelich** to full-time status. We continue to monitor **Hyeseong Kim** in the minors, but for today, the focus remains on leveraging the speed of **Caleb Durbin** (63.65) and the order-derived value of **Carson Benge** (56.72) to maintain our 5x5 standing.",
